Perfect! All tests now pass. 

The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second element) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element). Since Python lists are 0-indexed, the first word is at index 0, not index 1. This caused:
- `test_basic` to fail by returning 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `test_single` to error because there is no index 1 when the list only has one element

The fix was simple: change `parts[1]` to `parts[0]`.
